If `true`, do not call `writer.fail()` on error.

Returns: {Promise} Fulfills with the total number of bytes written.
Fulfills with the total number of bytes written.

`pipeToSync(source[, ...transforms], writer[, options])`
Synchronous version of pipeTo(). The source, all transforms, and the writer must be synchronous. Cannot accept async iterables or promises. 
The writer must have the *Sync methods (writeSync, writevSync, endSync) and fail() for this to work. 
pipeToSync() never falls back to the asynchronous writer methods. If writer.endSync() returns -1 because the writer cannot close synchronously (for example, a push() writer whose consumer has not read all of the data yet), pipeToSync() throws ERR_INVALID_STATE. All of the data was accepted by then, so by default the writer is not failed: it can still be closed, for example with await writer.end(). If the writer cannot be closed any other way (for example, it has no end() method), or the caller will not close it, set failOnIncompleteClose to fail it with the thrown error instead.
